t of NFC"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"application identifiers and a NFC Privacy statement to the application."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Wireless entitlement"}]}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Select your project."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Select your application target."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Choose the “Signing & Capabilities” tab."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Click the “+”-button to add a new capability."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Select the “Near Field Communication Tag” capability."}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"nfc-entitlement.png"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add list of NFC application identifiers"}]}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Choose the “Info” tab.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the “ISO7816 application identifiers for NFC” key to the “Custom iOS Target Properties”."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"start":6,"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"nfc-identifiers.png"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the Yubico NFC application identifiers to enable communication with the different","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"applications on the YubiKey.","type":"text"}]}]}],"start":8,"type":"orderedList"},{"syntax":null,"code":["A000000527471117  \/\/ YubiKey Management Application","A0000006472F0001  \/\/ FIDO\/U2F","A0000005272101    \/\/ OATH","A000000308        \/\/ PIV","A000000527200101  \/\/ YubiKey application\/OTP (for HMAC SHA1 challenge-response)","A000000151000000  \/\/ Security Domain"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"nfc-identifiers-list.png"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a NFC Privacy description"}]}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the “Privacy - NFC Usage Scan Description” key and a string that describes what you will use NFC for in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the application e.g “The application needs access to NFC reading to communicate with your YubiKey.”"}]}]}],"start":9},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"nfc-privacy.png"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"SmartCardUSB","text":"SmartCard\/USB"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To support YubiKeys connected via the USB port on a device running iOS 16 or higher, you need to add the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"com.apple.security.smartcard"},{"type":"text","text":" entitlement to your application."}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Select the application entitlements file."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"com.apple.security.smartcard"},{"type":"text","text":" entitlement to the entitlement list."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"smart-card.png"}]},{"name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"USB SmartCard supports Yubico OTP slot programming. HMAC-SHA1 challenge-response requires","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HIDOTPConnection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on macOS, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/LightningSmartCardConnection","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", or NFC without a touch requirement.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/YubiOTP\/Session","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"LightningAccessoryConnection-ie-5Ci-YubiKey","text":"Lightning\/AccessoryConnection i.e 5Ci YubiKey"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To add support for the 5Ci YubiKey that connect to the iPhone via the Lightning port you need to add the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"com.yubico.ylp"},{"type":"text","text":" string to the list of External Accessories."}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Select your project."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Select your application target."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Choose the “Info” tab."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If not present add the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Supported external accessory protocols"},{"type":"text","text":" key and insert the string "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"com.yubico.ylp"},{"type":"text","text":" in its list."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"external-accessory.png"}]},{"name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The YubiKey 5Ci is an Apple MFi certified external accessory and communicates over iAP2. Setting the value for ","type":"text"},{"code":"Supported external accessory protocols","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"code":"com.yubico.ylp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" will tell the app that all communication with the 5Ci YubiKey via the Lightning port is done using the External Accessory framework.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Making-Your-First-Connection","text":"Making Your First Connection"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now that your project is configured, you can start connecting to YubiKeys. YubiKit provides different connection types depending on how the YubiKey is connected to the device."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Understanding-Connection-Types","text":"Understanding Connection Types"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"YubiKit provides the following connection methods:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"NFC"}]},{"text":": Short-range wireless communication (iOS only)","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"USB"}]},{"text":": Direct USB connection via SmartCard interface","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lightning"}]},{"text":": YubiKey 5Ci connected to Lightning port (iOS only)","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"USB HID"}]},{"text":": Direct access to the FIDO or OTP interface (macOS only)","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each connection type works differently, so let’s explore how to use them.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"NFC-Connections","text":"NFC Connections"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"NFC connections are user-initiated and short-lived. The user must bring their YubiKey close to their device:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import YubiKit","","\/\/ Start an NFC scan","do {","    let connection = try await NFCSmartCardConnection()","","    \/\/ Use the connection quickly - NFC sessions have a timeout","    let session = try await OATHSession.makeSession(connection: connection)","    let codes = try await session.calculateCredentialCodes()","","    \/\/ Always close NFC connections with a user message","    await connection.close(message: \"OATH codes retrieved\")","","} catch {","    \/\/ Handle connection errors (user cancelled, no YubiKey found, etc.)","    print(\"NFC connection failed: \\(error)\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"NFC connections automatically show the iOS NFC interface and require user interaction to complete.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"USB-and-Lightning-Connections","text":"USB and Lightning Connections"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Wired connections are persistent - they stay connected until the YubiKey is unplugged:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import YubiKit","","\/\/ Connect to any wired YubiKey (USB or Lightning)","do {","    let connection = try await WiredSmartCardConnection.makeConnection()","","    \/\/ Perform operations - connection stays active","    let session = try await OATHSession.makeSession(connection: connection)","    let codes = try await session.calculateCredentialCodes()","","    \/\/ Monitor for disconnection or close when done","    let error = await connection.waitUntilClosed()","    if let error = error {","        print(\"Connection closed with error: \\(error)\")","    }","","} catch {","    print(\"Wired connection failed: \\(error)\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"WiredSmartCardConnection.makeConnection()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method automatically detects whether you’re using USB or Lightning.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Specific-Connection-Types","text":"Specific Connection Types"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For more control, you can connect to specific interfaces:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ USB only","let usbConnection = try await USBSmartCardConnection()","","\/\/ Lightning only (iOS)","let lightningConnection = try await LightningSmartCardConnection()","","\/\/ NFC with custom message (iOS)","let nfcConnection = try await NFCSmartCardConnection(","    alertMessage: \"Hold your YubiKey near the phone\"",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On macOS, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"HIDOTPConnection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the OTP keyboard interface or ","type":"text"},{"code":"HIDFIDOConnection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the FIDO interface:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let otpConnection = try await HIDOTPConnection()"]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Understanding-Connection-Lifecycle","text":"Understanding Connection Lifecycle"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Critical:"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Connections must be explicitly closed. You can only have one active connection to a YubiKey at any time.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Connection-Behavior","text":"Connection Behavior"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exclusive access"}]},{"text":": Only one connection can exist per YubiKey at any time","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Manual closure required"}]},{"text":": Dropping a connection reference does NOT automatically close it - you must call ","type":"text"},{"code":"close()","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Resource blocking"}]},{"text":": An unclosed connection prevents new connections (throws ","type":"text"},{"code":"SmartCardConnectionError.busy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each connection is a lightweight value type that identifies an active hardware session. Copying a connection creates another handle to the same session, not a new connection - the hardware is only released when you call ","type":"text"},{"code":"close()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Working-with-Sessions","text":"Working with Sessions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Once you have a connection, create sessions to access different YubiKey applications:","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"OATH-Session-TOTPHOTP-codes","text":"OATH Session (TOTP\/HOTP codes)"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let session = try await OATHSession.makeSession(connection: connection)","let codes = try await session.calculateCredentialCodes()","","for (credential, code) in codes {","    print(\"\\(credential.label): \\(code?.code ?? \"Touch required\")\")","}"]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Yubico-OTP-Session-OTP-slots","text":"Yubico OTP Session (OTP slots)"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/YubiOTP\/Session","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" manages the two OTP slots. Create it with a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/SmartCardConnection","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" or,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on macOS, an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/OTPConnection","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let session = try await YubiOTP.Session.makeSession(connection: connection)","let state = await session.configState","print(\"Slot 2 configured: \\(try state.isConfigured(.two))\")","","\/\/ Program slot 2 for HOTP, replacing its existing configuration","try await session.putConfiguration(.hotp(key: secret), in: .two)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/YubiOTP\/Session","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for HMAC-SHA1 challenge-response, transport support, and NFC output.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"PIV-Session-Certificates-and-keys","text":"PIV Session (Certificates and keys)"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let session = try await PIVSession.makeSession(connection: connection)","let certificate = try await session.getCertificate(in: .authentication)","print(\"Found certificate: \\(certificate.subject)\")"]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Management-Session-Device-information","text":"Management Session (Device information)"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let session: Management.Session = try await .makeSession(connection: connection)","print(\"YubiKey version: \\(await session.version)\")","","let deviceInfo = try await session.getDeviceInfo()","print(\"Device info: \\(deviceInfo)\")"]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"WebAuthn-Client-FIDO2--passkeys","text":"WebAuthn Client (FIDO2 \/ passkeys)"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For passkey registration and authentication, "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" wraps a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/CTAP2\/Session","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and runs the W3C ceremonies end-to-end. CTAP2 sessions can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HIDFIDOConnection"},{"type":"text","text":" (USB HID on macOS) or any "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/SmartCardConnection","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(NFC \/ USB CCID)."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let connection = try await HIDFIDOConnection()","let session = try await CTAP2.Session.makeSession(connection: connection)","","let client = WebAuthn.Client(","    session: session,","    origin: try .init(\"https:\/\/example.com\"),","    isPublicSuffix: { publicSuffixList.contains($0) }",")","","let response = try await client.makeCredential(","    .init(","        challenge: challenge,","        rp: .init(id: \"example.com\", name: \"Example\"),","        user: .init(id: userId, name: \"alice@example.com\")","    ),","    authorization: .pin(\"1234\")",").value"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"PIN and UV are supplied per ceremony via "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Authorization","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". For raw"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"CTAP2 access (credential management, bio enrollment, large blobs), use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/CTAP2\/Session","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" directly."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Connection-Management-Patterns","text":"Connection Management Patterns"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"For-UI-Applications","text":"For UI Applications"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In SwiftUI or UIKit apps, you typically want to maintain persistent connections and react to connection changes. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/OATHSampleCode","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for complete examples of reactive connection management patterns that automatically update your UI when YubiKeys are plugged in or removed."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"For-Command-Line-Tools","text":"For Command-Line Tools"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"CLI applications often use a simpler approach with a single connection per operation. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/PIVToolSampleCode","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for examples of how command-line tools handle connections for one-time operations."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Next-Steps","text":"Next Steps"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now you’re ready to build YubiKey applications! Check out the sample projects to see complete implementations:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OATHSample"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Shows how to build a TOTP authenticator app with SwiftUI"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"PIVTool"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Demonstrates PIV operations for certificates and digital signatures"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"WebAuthnInterceptorSample"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Routes WebAuthn calls from a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WKWebView"},{"type":"text","text":" through "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client"},{"type":"text","text":" to a YubiKey"}]}]}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Build-SDK-documentation","text":"Build SDK documentation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","tex